The trouble with a 3D view for NH is that NH doesn't currently have any
notion of "direction faced".  A player who could only see in one
direction would be SEVERELY disadvantaged.  To be playable, you would
need to add proximity sound effects for creatures and effects behind
the player, and fast, high-quality changing of direction, and a
wide-angle view (150 or so degrees - letterbox).  

Another factor is Time.  Will it seem strange for the player to have
realtime direction changing, but non-realtime movement (ie. you take a
step and all the monsters take a step, then everything is still while
you look around).

As for actual implementation, I can't see many difficulties, once you
have a 3D display engine, as the WindowPort interface of NH is quite
good.

